            "buttonSize": "big",
            "goToSlideType": "specified",
            "invisible": false,
            "solution": ""
          },
          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 13.245033112582782,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Domestic Policies</strong><br>\nUnder Brezhnev, the Soviet Union experienced a period of economic stagnation. However, he is credited with improving the standard of living and maintaining a stable society.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Foreign Policy</strong><br>\nBrezhnev's foreign policy was marked by the expansion of Soviet influence in Eastern Europe and increased tension with the West, culminating in the period known as détente and the signing of the Helsinki Accords.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Arms Race and Afghanistan</strong><br>\nHe presided over the Soviet Union during the height of the Cold War, overseeing an arms race with the United States. In 1979, he made the decision to invade Afghanistan, a move that proved to be politically and militarily costly.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "3b13867b-feab-4e2e-bfa2-fcc82e4dbff1"
            },
